FlightTrack uses data and software from the following third parties.

Aircraft positions
  adsb.fi open data API — https://adsb.fi
    Personal, non-commercial use only. Attribution required. Limit: one request per second.
  adsb.lol API (fallback) and daily traces (where a flight was last seen) — https://adsb.lol
    Data under the Open Database License (ODbL).

Used only with the user's own key or account (Settings, Feeds), under that account's terms
  The OpenSky Network REST API — https://opensky-network.org
    Free account (OAuth2 client credentials); credit limits per day. Cite OpenSky where its
    data is used in published work.
  FlightAware AeroAPI, Personal tier — https://www.flightaware.com/commercial/aeroapi/
    Personal and academic use only; paid by the request beyond a monthly credit.
  ADS-B Exchange Community API, through RapidAPI — https://www.adsbexchange.com
    Non-commercial use; a monthly allowance of requests.

Maps and weather
  Esri World Imagery and World Boundaries and Places — https://www.esri.com
    Sources: Esri, Maxar, Earthstar Geographics, and the GIS User Community.
  NEXRAD radar composite, Iowa Environmental Mesonet, Iowa State University
    — https://mesonet.agron.iastate.edu
  RainViewer weather radar (outside the contiguous United States) — https://www.rainviewer.com
  GeoColor satellite imagery, NASA Global Imagery Browse Services (GIBS)
    — https://earthdata.nasa.gov/gibs
  Esri World Street Map — https://www.esri.com
  VFR sectional charts, Federal Aviation Administration, Aeronautical Information Services
    (tile service; United States only; not for navigation) — https://adds-faa.opendata.arcgis.com
  Class airspace boundaries, Federal Aviation Administration — https://adds-faa.opendata.arcgis.com

Airport weather
  METAR reports, Aviation Weather Center, US National Weather Service
    — https://aviationweather.gov

Aircraft details
  adsbdb.com API: routes by callsign, airframe details by hex code — https://www.adsbdb.com
  airport-data.com thumbnail API: aircraft photos, credited to their photographers on screen
    — https://airport-data.com

Ground elevation (the coverage map shown with diagnostics)
  Open-Meteo Elevation API — https://open-meteo.com
    Free for non-commercial use, CC BY 4.0. Data: Copernicus DEM GLO-90, produced using
    Copernicus WorldDEM-90 (c) DLR e.V. 2010-2014 and (c) Airbus Defence and Space GmbH
    2014-2018, provided under COPERNICUS by the European Union and ESA.

Location
  OurAirports airport and runway data (public domain), bundled — https://ourairports.com/data/
  ipinfo.io IP geolocation, asked once at start-up for the Current Location favorite — https://ipinfo.io

Software
  pygame-ce (LGPL-2.1) — https://pyga.me
  Requests (Apache-2.0) — https://requests.readthedocs.io
  Flask (BSD-3-Clause) — https://flask.palletsprojects.com
